      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should frame the 5% as a foundational success that demonstrates initial viability, not a final metric. Instead of focusing on the percentage, emphasize the *qualitative* achievements, such as the successful implementation of novel restoration techniques or the establishment of critical community partnerships. Furthermore, you can strategically position the 5% as the baseline from which your next, larger phase of work—funded by this grant—will achieve exponential growth. This narrative shifts the focus from past shortfall to future, guaranteed success.",
